' This diagram is intended to illustrate the processes carried out by a user and the system to achieve the "Safe Return to Home" use case.
' In the 'Safe Return to Home' use case, the user requests a safe route home, and the system computes and provides a recommended route based on real-time context data.
[ ] Debe haber un escenario 0 que muestre un mapa por defecto

@startuml
    actor       "User" as User
    participant "User Interface" as UI
    participant "API Layer" as API
    participant "Routing Engine" as RE
    participant "Context Analyzer" as CA
    participant "Data Management" as DM
    participant "Map Source" as MapAPI
    participant "Meteo Data Source" as Meteo
    participant "Open Data Source" as OpenData

    User --> UI : Go Home request

    UI --> API : RouteRequest\n(origin, destination, preferences)

    API --> RE : calculate_routes(request)

    RE --> DM : getGraphData(area)
    DM --> MapAPI : fetchMapData(area)
    DM --> RE : GraphData

    RE --> CA : evaluateRoutes(RouteCandidates)

    CA --> DM : getWeatherData(time)
    DM --> Meteo : fetchWeatherData(...)
    Meteo --> DM : WeatherData

    CA --> DM : getUrbanData(area)
    DM --> OpenData : fetchUrbanData(...)
    OpenData --> DM : UrbanData

    CA --> RE : RouteScores

    API --> UI : RouteResponse\n(routes + safety/comfort scores)

    UI --> API : MapRequest(area, zoom)
    API --> DM : getMapView(request)
    DM --> MapAPI : fetchMapData(area)
    MapAPI --> DM : Map tiles + metadata
    API --> UI : MapDataResponse

    UI --> User : Display routes on map\nwith "Safe rating" scores
@enduml

